{"parentUuid":"7c035b0b-7643-4d08-9de7-62f47ab0ab7d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f207c52e-9ba4-4c71-8087-58bd5a5cf263","agentId":"ab1c8a4a09fa5a796","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019QDvEXL6sTydqQv2rSrEPd","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a1c405674f8d75f7a (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a1c405674f8d75f7a', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\tasks\\a1c405674f8d75f7a.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"afd98e62-4186-413d-8a9f-1feb9e5043d9","timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:30:28.420Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7c035b0b-7643-4d08-9de7-62f47ab0ab7d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
{"parentUuid":"afd98e62-4186-413d-8a9f-1feb9e5043d9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab1c8a4a09fa5a796","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfcEFZMLkgjmGEYkmvmWV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wy665uwdLi3pW9q1rNDJRy","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research fan, filter, heat data","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Research task (web, read-only; load tools via ToolSearch \"select:WebSearch,WebFetch\"). Do NOT download files, do not write any files. Return a compact sourced answer (every number with source URL; mark anything not found as NOT FOUND, never invent).\n\nContext: a stainless enclosed cabinet (inner ~1497 x 315 x 855 mm, i.e. ~0.40 m3) sits above a conveyor pizza oven; an uninsulated 304 steel flue extension (300 x 200 mm rectangular, 336 mm long) of the oven exhaust passes through it. We need forced ventilation with 24 V fans and a ~35 W electrical panel inside must stay <= 50 °C when the shop is 38–44 °C. Also an oven-top extraction hood box needs a real duct fan and grease filter.\n\nFind:\n1. ebm-papst 4414 FL (and 4414 F / 4414 FN if FL not listed): exact dimensions (119x119x25?), voltage, air flow m3/h, power W, max ambient temperature, noise. Official ebm-papst page/datasheet.\n2. A real radial/centrifugal duct fan suitable for a 300 x 200 mm rectangular duct OR a compact centrifugal blower with spiral housing (ebm-papst, Systemair, Ziehl-Abegg, Soler&Palau), air flow 300–600 m3/h, permissible medium temperature >= 60 °C (ideally 80–120 °C for kitchen exhaust): model name, outer dimensions (L x W x H, inlet/outlet sizes), weight, power, voltage, max air temperature. Two or three candidates; Systemair KT 30-15 / KE 30-15 / KVK / MUB, or ebm-papst RadiPac / R2E ... whichever has a datasheet with dimensions.\n3. EN 16282-6 stainless baffle (labyrinth) grease filter: standard sizes (e.g. 400x250x25? 500x400x50?), manufacturer example with datasheet (e.g. Systemair, Elica, Lamier, Hood filters), nominal air flow per filter and pressure drop.\n4. Phoenix Contact QUINT4-CAP supercapacitor DC-UPS 24 V (order no., energy kJ, output current, buffer time at ~25 W, dimensions W x H x D, operating temperature range). Also RevPi Connect 4 and RevPi DIO operating temperature range (revolutionpi.com), Mean Well NDR-120-24 operating temp/derating.\n5. A DIN-rail enclosure thermostat for fan control (e.g. STEGO KTS 011 / KTO 011, Rittal SK 3110) – dimensions, contact rating; and a simple DIN-rail/ panel temperature sensor readable by a PLC (e.g. PT100 / 4–20 mA transmitter) - one example with dims.\n6. Heat transfer data: rock wool (stone wool) pipe/duct insulation thermal conductivity at 100 °C and 200 °C (e.g. ROCKWOOL ProRox), typical exhaust flue gas temperature at outlet of an electric conveyor pizza oven (Middleby Marshall / Zanolli / Sveba Dahlen / Lincoln Impinger) or any electric conveyor oven exhaust temperature measurement; natural convection heat transfer coefficient for vertical/horizontal plate (typical 4–8 W/m2K) and stainless steel emissivity (~0.1–0.3 polished/brushed).\n7. VRLA 24 V lead-acid battery: maximum recommended ambient temperature and lifetime halving rule (e.g. Yuasa/CSB datasheet), to justify replacing it with supercaps.\n\nAnswer in <= 60 lines, grouped by numbered item.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":364369,"output_tokens":4045,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1024},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1017},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4045,"cache_read_input_tokens":364369,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1017,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Wy665uwdLi3pW9q1rNDJRy":{"description":"Research fan, filter, heat data","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Research task (web, read-only; load tools via ToolSearch \"select:WebSearch,WebFetch\"). Do NOT download files, do not write any files. Return a compact sourced answer (every number with source URL; mark anything not found as NOT FOUND, never invent).\n\nContext: a stainless enclosed cabinet (inner ~1497 x 315 x 855 mm, i.e. ~0.40 m3) sits above a conveyor pizza oven; an uninsulated 304 steel flue extension (300 x 200 mm rectangular, 336 mm long) of the oven exhaust passes through it. We need forced ventilation with 24 V fans and a ~35 W electrical panel inside must stay <= 50 °C when the shop is 38–44 °C. Also an oven-top extraction hood box needs a real duct fan and grease filter.\n\nFind:\n1. ebm-papst 4414 FL (and 4414 F / 4414 FN if FL not listed): exact dimensions (119x119x25?), voltage, air flow m3/h, power W, max ambient temperature, noise. Official ebm-papst page/datasheet.\n2. A real radial/centrifugal duct fan suitable for a 300 x 200 mm rectangular duct OR a compact centrifugal blower with spiral housing (ebm-papst, Systemair, Ziehl-Abegg, Soler&Palau), air flow 300–600 m3/h, permissible medium temperature >= 60 °C (ideally 80–120 °C for kitchen exhaust): model name, outer dimensions (L x W x H, inlet/outlet sizes), weight, power, voltage, max air temperature. Two or three candidates; Systemair KT 30-15 / KE 30-15 / KVK / MUB, or ebm-papst RadiPac / R2E ... whichever has a datasheet with dimensions.\n3. EN 16282-6 stainless baffle (labyrinth) grease filter: standard sizes (e.g. 400x250x25? 500x400x50?), manufacturer example with datasheet (e.g. Systemair, Elica, Lamier, Hood filters), nominal air flow per filter and pressure drop.\n4. Phoenix Contact QUINT4-CAP supercapacitor DC-UPS 24 V (order no., energy kJ, output current, buffer time at ~25 W, dimensions W x H x D, operating temperature range). Also RevPi Connect 4 and RevPi DIO operating temperature range (revolutionpi.com), Mean Well NDR-120-24 operating temp/derating.\n5. A DIN-rail enclosure thermostat for fan control (e.g. STEGO KTS 011 / KTO 011, Rittal SK 3110) – dimensions, contact rating; and a simple DIN-rail/ panel temperature sensor readable by a PLC (e.g. PT100 / 4–20 mA transmitter) - one example with dims.\n6. Heat transfer data: rock wool (stone wool) pipe/duct insulation thermal conductivity at 100 °C and 200 °C (e.g. ROCKWOOL ProRox), typical exhaust flue gas temperature at outlet of an electric conveyor pizza oven (Middleby Marshall / Zanolli / Sveba Dahlen / Lincoln Impinger) or any electric conveyor oven exhaust temperature measurement; natural convection heat transfer coefficient for vertical/horizontal plate (typical 4–8 W/m2K) and stainless steel emissivity (~0.1–0.3 polished/brushed).\n7. VRLA 24 V lead-acid battery: maximum recommended ambient temperature and lifetime halving rule (e.g. Yuasa/CSB datasheet), to justify replacing it with supercaps.\n\nAnswer in <= 60 lines, grouped by numbered item.","run_in_background":true}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfcEFYUFWNtiEfmQmRc9q","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e81f630-08c1-43a7-a88a-4e984949b7e6","timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:30:43.184Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
