{"parentUuid":"41c09689-7a8a-43c5-9320-9af14ef160d5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"656b2f0e-eedd-4eb4-a289-250634ab97ab","agentId":"ab1c8a4a09fa5a796","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RojDvjjD7RkVyMsSTLkb4z","type":"tool_result","content":"-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121 2645176 Sep 30 21:03 5p650i.stp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121     674 Sep 30 21:03 5p650i.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121  222226 Sep 30 21:03 hgh15ca.stp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121    1000 Sep 30 21:03 hgh15ca.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121  439690 Sep 30 21:03 ndr-240-24.stp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121     596 Sep 30 21:03 ndr-240-24.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121  304954 Sep 30 21:03 pgcn23-1025.step\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121     988 Sep 30 21:03 pgcn23-1025.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121 7818395 Sep 30 21:03 stp-drv-4830.step\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121 3328868 Sep 30 21:03 stp-drv-4850.step\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121 9216678 Sep 30 21:03 stp-drvac-24025.step\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121 5979684 Sep 30 21:03 stp-mtr-23079.step\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121  940416 Sep 30 21:03 stp-mtrac-23078.step\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121     914 Sep 30 21:03 stp-mtrac-23078.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121 8801119 Sep 30 21:03 ub10-242.stp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121     659 Sep 30 21:03 ub10-242.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121  258948 Sep 30 21:03 w2e200-hh38-01.stp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121     817 Sep 30 21:03 w2e200-hh38-01.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121  641543 Sep 30 21:03 xu080149.stp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Kemal 197121     632 Sep 30 21:03 xu080149.txt","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2dd3593e-fb29-461e-93f6-ea92e0b36bab","timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:46:15.728Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"41c09689-7a8a-43c5-9320-9af14ef160d5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
{"parentUuid":"2dd3593e-fb29-461e-93f6-ea92e0b36bab","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab1c8a4a09fa5a796","attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4269a801e06a0d24</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Wy665uwdLi3pW9q1rNDJRy</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\tasks\\a4269a801e06a0d24.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Research fan, filter, heat data\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I found most of what you asked for, but four things are missing: an exhaust temperature at the flue of an electric conveyor oven, an official ebm-papst 4414 FN sheet, a manufacturer baffle-filter curve that cites EN 16282-6, and a \"brushed stainless\" emissivity. The WebFetch name lookup kept failing on some hosts, so a few values below come only from search-result text and are marked (snippet). Numbers marked (derived) are my own arithmetic.\n\n**1. ebm-papst 4414 F series (official datasheets, all 119×119×25 mm, 0.175 kg)**\n- **4414 FL:** 24 VDC (18–28 V), 1600 rpm, 1.2 W, 94 m³/h, 26 dB(A), −20…+75 °C. Life (L10) is 80 000 h at 40 °C and 35 000 h at maximum temperature. Speed signal output. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414FL-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 F:** 24 V (12–28 V), 2900 rpm, 5.0 W, 170 m³/h, 43 dB(A), maximum 60 °C, L10 60 000 h / 37 500 h. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414F-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 FM:** 2400 rpm, 3.1 W, 140 m³/h, 38 dB(A), maximum 75 °C, L10 70 000 h / 30 000 h. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414FM-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 N:** note it is 119×119×**38** mm. 3650 rpm, 5.4 W, 205 m³/h, 46 dB(A), maximum 70 °C. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414N-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 FN:** NOT FOUND. The official URL returns 404.\n\n**2. Duct fans and blowers.** None is made for 300×200; the two rectangular ones are 300×150 and need a transition piece.\n- **(a) ebm-papst G1G140-AV17-02**, 24 VDC blower with spiral housing and flange:\n  - 16–28 V, 54 W, 2.5 A, 1750 rpm, 2.3 kg, IP22, 0–10 V/PWM input plus speed output.\n  - Maximum ambient (and therefore air) temperature is **60 °C**, so it is not suitable for hot hood exhaust.\n  - Outside size max. 227.8×262.6 mm. A distributor listing gives 130 mm depth and about 400 m³/h (235.4 CFM).\n  - https://mm.digikey.com/Volume0/opasdata/d220001/medias/docus/6163/EBMPapstG1G140AV1702datasheet.pdf · https://us.rs-online.com/product/ebm-papst/g1g140-av17-02/70393924/\n- **(b) Systemair RS 30-15 sileo** (item 77284), 300×150 rectangular duct fan:\n  - 230 V, 51 W, 0.224 A, 464 m³/h max, **70 °C** max air temperature (also when speed-controlled), 6.2 kg, IP44.\n  - Dimension letters A–L: 402 / 217 / 340 / 190 / 320 / 170 / 298 / 148 / 79 / 120 / 230 / 254 mm.\n  - Example operating point: 210 m³/h at 228 Pa, 50.8 W.\n  - https://en.ventilatory.net/media/catalog/product/data/ds-rs-30-15-sileo-en.pdf\n- **(c) Soler&amp;Palau IRB/2-180**, 300×150 rectangular duct fan:\n  - 63 W, 0.14 m³/s (504 m³/h), −30…+70 °C, 10 kg.\n  - Table as printed: A1 300, A2 150, B1 320, B2 170, C1 340, C2 190, H1 200, H2 480, L 375 mm.\n  - https://statics.solerpalau.com/media/import/documentation/FINAL_FANS_FOR_FOOD_SERVICE_2020_EDITION_2.pdf (catalogue page 17)\n- **(d) Systemair KBT 160EC** (item 454440), kitchen box fan, **120 °C continuous**:\n  - 230 V, 171 W, 928 m³/h max, 26 kg, Ø160 inlet, 50 mm mineral wool, 0–10 V control, IP55.\n  - Dimension letters: A 437, B 384, C 249, D 212, H 473, I 470, M 345, P 320 mm.\n  - Example operating point: 418 m³/h at 166 Pa, 79.7 W.\n  - https://en.ventilatory.net/media/catalog/product/data/ds-kbt-160-ec-en.pdf\n  - The AC version KBT 160E4 is 832 m³/h, 121 W, 24.9 kg: https://en.ventilatory.net/kbt-160e4.html\n- **Systemair KE/KT:** I found no 30-15 size. KT 40-20 is rated 55 °C (snippet).\n\n**3. Grease (flame-protection) filters**\n- **EN 16282-6 F-1 (type A), 500×500×25 mm:** AISI 304, 500 m³/h at 100 Pa, 4.5 kg. A 40 mm-deep version also exists. https://www.gastroplus24.de/de/flammenschutzfilter-typ-a-500-x-500-x-25-mm-ffa505010\n- **EN 16282-6 F-2 (type B), 500×500×20 mm:** 600 m³/h at 50 Pa, 2.4 kg. https://www.gastroplus24.de/de/flammschutzfilter-bauart-b-500-x-500-x-20-mm-nach-din-en-16282-6-f-2/FFO5050-10\n- **Baffle 495×495×45 mm (DIN 18869-5):** 25 Pa at 0.4 m/s, 50 Pa at 0.6 m/s, 80 Pa at 0.7 m/s. At 0.6 m/s that is about 530 m³/h (derived). https://www.ecanopy.co.uk/Box-6-Grease-Filters-Baffle-Commercial-495mm\n- **Manufacturer datasheet (Systemair / Elica / Lamier) with full curves citing EN 16282-6:** NOT FOUND.\n\n**4. Backup power and controller**\n- **Phoenix Contact QUINT4-CAP/24DC/5/4KJ, order no. 2320539:**\n  - 4 kJ in double-layer capacitors, 5 A output.\n  - Buffer time 3 min at 1 A and 30 s at 5 A. At about 25 W (≈1 A) that means roughly 3 min.\n  - 94×130×125 mm (W×H×D), 1243 g, needs 50 mm clearance top and bottom.\n  - Operating −25…+60 °C, derated 1 %/K above 40 °C.\n  - https://dienelectric.com/pdf/Phoenix-Contact-QUINT4-CAP-24DC-5-4KJ---2320539-Datasheet.pdf\n- **RevPi Connect 4:** approved −25…+55 °C, 96×45×110.5 mm, max 20 W. https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Technical_Datasheet_RevPi_Connect-4.pdf\n  - Kunbus says 55 °C is where the processor starts slowing down under load: https://revolutionpi.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=4619\n- **RevPi DIO (100197):** −40…+55 °C, 96×22.5×110.5 mm, 1.5 W, 14 inputs / 14 outputs, 500 mA per output (high-side). https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Datasheet_RevPi_DIO.pdf\n- **Mean Well NDR-120-24:**\n  - Working range −20…+70 °C per its derating curve, 40×125.2×113.5 mm.\n  - Read from the curve drawing (derived): 100 % load from −10 to 50 °C, then straight down to 50 % at 70 °C.\n  - https://docs.rs-online.com/a255/0900766b81621f96.pdf\n\n**5. Thermostats and temperature sensor**\n- **STEGO KTS 011, 01141.0-00** (normally open, closes on rising temperature, 0…60 °C):\n  - 60×33×43 mm, 40 g, 35 mm DIN rail clip, IP20, −45…+80 °C.\n  - Contacts: AC 250 V 10(2) A, AC 120 V 15(2) A, DC 24–72 V 30 W.\n  - Switching difference 7 K ±4 K. The normally-closed version is KTO 011, 01140.0-00.\n  - https://www.tme.eu/Document/9b800d1efeb6c8442e3857b41402ae2b/KTO011_KTS011_EN.pdf\n- **Rittal SK 3110.000:** 71×71×33.5 mm, set range 5…60 °C, change-over contact.\n  - AC 10(4) A heating / AC 5(4) A cooling, DC max 30 W.\n  - Switching difference about 1 K ±0.8 K; 24–230 V AC or 24–60 V DC; 0.105 kg.\n  - https://docs.rs-online.com/49de/A700000008467962.pdf\n- **Sensor option 1, RevPi AIO (100250):** 2 Pt100/Pt1000 inputs (2-, 3- or 4-wire), 96×22.5×110.5 mm, −30…+55 °C. https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Datasheet_RevPi_AIO.pdf\n- **Sensor option 2, Phoenix Contact MINI MCR-SL-PT100-UI-200-NC (2864370):**\n  - 6.2×93.1×102.5 mm, 19.2–30 V DC, &lt;500 mW.\n  - Pt100 input −50…+200 °C (set by switches), 4–20 mA and other outputs.\n  - −20…+65 °C, error &lt;0.3 %.\n  - https://datasheet.octopart.com/2864370-Phoenix-Contact-datasheet-95109.pdf\n\n**6. Heat-transfer data**\n- **ROCKWOOL ProRox PS 960 (ASTM C335):** λ = 0.036 W/mK at 38 °C, 0.042 at 93 °C, 0.050 at 149 °C, 0.058 at 204 °C. Maximum use temperature 649 °C. https://rti.rockwool.com/siteassets/applications/wr-tech/rw-ti-prorox-ps-960-wr-tech_en.pdf\n  - The EN figures (0.046 at 100 °C, 0.064 at 200 °C) are snippet only.\n- **Exhaust temperature at the flue of an electric conveyor oven: NOT FOUND.** Closest data:\n  - Middleby PS638: bakes at 163–316 °C.\n  - Middleby PS638: gives off 15.2 kW to the room at steady 500 °F, 16.0 kW while cooking.\n  - Middleby PS638: oven top skin up to 76.1 °C.\n  - Source: https://www.middlebymarshall.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DOC-1010A-MM-PS638-Ventless-Submittal-Package.pdf\n  - Zanolli Synthesis: maximum set point 320 °C. https://static.ggmgastro.com/Grill_Pizzeria/pizzaofen/dpz/SY1165.E.D.UK.08.rev.0.4_Neutro.pdf\n- **Natural convection in air (laminar):** h = C·(ΔT/L)^0.25, with C = 1.42 for a vertical plate, 1.32 for a horizontal plate heated on top, 0.59 heated underneath. https://www.electronics-cooling.com/2001/08/simplified-formula-for-estimating-natural-convection-heat-transfer-coefficient-on-a-flat-plate/\n  - Example (derived): ΔT 10 K on an 855 mm wall gives h ≈ 2.6 W/m²K.\n  - A vertical plate at ΔT 30 K is about 5 W/m²K (engineersedge, snippet).\n- **Stainless steel emissivity:** polished 0.075, weathered 0.85, type 301 0.54–0.63, at about 300 K. https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/emissivity-coefficients-d_447.html\n  - Buffed 18-8 is 0.16 (snippet). A \"brushed\" value: NOT FOUND.\n\n**7. VRLA battery (why to switch to supercaps)**\n- **CSB GP1272:** nominal 25 °C; discharge −15…50 °C; charge and storage −15…**40 °C**. Design life up to 5 years standby at 25 °C (3–5 years by the European rating). https://csb-battery.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/CSB-Datasheet-GP1272-12V25W-%E2%80%93-053124.pdf\n- **Life halving:** Yuasa says life halves for every 10 °C rise (valid about 15–40 °C) — snippet. https://www.blueboxbatteries.co.uk/assets/yuasa-battery-care-110b.pdf\n  - Schneider gives about 50 % less life per 10 °C above 25 °C (snippet). https://blog.se.com/digital-transformation/it-management/2014/08/28/recommendations-prolonging-life-ups-battery/\n\nWhat this means for the design:\n- A battery charging in a 44–50 °C cabinet is outside CSB's 40 °C charging limit.\n- QUINT4-CAP, NDR-120 and RevPi all work up to 50 °C. The tightest limit is 55 °C, set by the RevPi Connect 4 and DIO.\n- Of the fans, only the KBT 160EC (120 °C) suits the hot hood. The G1G140 (60 °C) and RS 30-15 / IRB (70 °C) are for cooler air only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>249385</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>153</tool_uses><duration_ms>877340</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","source_uuid":"8bb05899-4312-46b7-bd47-c906a49cde53","commandMode":"task-notification","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task"},"timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:45:20.530Z","usage":{"totalTokens":249385,"toolUses":153,"durationMs":877340}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7e29c759-be3d-42dc-afb3-95187ec92a9d","timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:45:20.530Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4269a801e06a0d24</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Wy665uwdLi3pW9q1rNDJRy</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\tasks\\a4269a801e06a0d24.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Research fan, filter, heat data\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I found most of what you asked for, but four things are missing: an exhaust temperature at the flue of an electric conveyor oven, an official ebm-papst 4414 FN sheet, a manufacturer baffle-filter curve that cites EN 16282-6, and a \"brushed stainless\" emissivity. The WebFetch name lookup kept failing on some hosts, so a few values below come only from search-result text and are marked (snippet). Numbers marked (derived) are my own arithmetic.\n\n**1. ebm-papst 4414 F series (official datasheets, all 119×119×25 mm, 0.175 kg)**\n- **4414 FL:** 24 VDC (18–28 V), 1600 rpm, 1.2 W, 94 m³/h, 26 dB(A), −20…+75 °C. Life (L10) is 80 000 h at 40 °C and 35 000 h at maximum temperature. Speed signal output. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414FL-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 F:** 24 V (12–28 V), 2900 rpm, 5.0 W, 170 m³/h, 43 dB(A), maximum 60 °C, L10 60 000 h / 37 500 h. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414F-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 FM:** 2400 rpm, 3.1 W, 140 m³/h, 38 dB(A), maximum 75 °C, L10 70 000 h / 30 000 h. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414FM-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 N:** note it is 119×119×**38** mm. 3650 rpm, 5.4 W, 205 m³/h, 46 dB(A), maximum 70 °C. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414N-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 FN:** NOT FOUND. The official URL returns 404.\n\n**2. Duct fans and blowers.** None is made for 300×200; the two rectangular ones are 300×150 and need a transition piece.\n- **(a) ebm-papst G1G140-AV17-02**, 24 VDC blower with spiral housing and flange:\n  - 16–28 V, 54 W, 2.5 A, 1750 rpm, 2.3 kg, IP22, 0–10 V/PWM input plus speed output.\n  - Maximum ambient (and therefore air) temperature is **60 °C**, so it is not suitable for hot hood exhaust.\n  - Outside size max. 227.8×262.6 mm. A distributor listing gives 130 mm depth and about 400 m³/h (235.4 CFM).\n  - https://mm.digikey.com/Volume0/opasdata/d220001/medias/docus/6163/EBMPapstG1G140AV1702datasheet.pdf · https://us.rs-online.com/product/ebm-papst/g1g140-av17-02/70393924/\n- **(b) Systemair RS 30-15 sileo** (item 77284), 300×150 rectangular duct fan:\n  - 230 V, 51 W, 0.224 A, 464 m³/h max, **70 °C** max air temperature (also when speed-controlled), 6.2 kg, IP44.\n  - Dimension letters A–L: 402 / 217 / 340 / 190 / 320 / 170 / 298 / 148 / 79 / 120 / 230 / 254 mm.\n  - Example operating point: 210 m³/h at 228 Pa, 50.8 W.\n  - https://en.ventilatory.net/media/catalog/product/data/ds-rs-30-15-sileo-en.pdf\n- **(c) Soler&amp;Palau IRB/2-180**, 300×150 rectangular duct fan:\n  - 63 W, 0.14 m³/s (504 m³/h), −30…+70 °C, 10 kg.\n  - Table as printed: A1 300, A2 150, B1 320, B2 170, C1 340, C2 190, H1 200, H2 480, L 375 mm.\n  - https://statics.solerpalau.com/media/import/documentation/FINAL_FANS_FOR_FOOD_SERVICE_2020_EDITION_2.pdf (catalogue page 17)\n- **(d) Systemair KBT 160EC** (item 454440), kitchen box fan, **120 °C continuous**:\n  - 230 V, 171 W, 928 m³/h max, 26 kg, Ø160 inlet, 50 mm mineral wool, 0–10 V control, IP55.\n  - Dimension letters: A 437, B 384, C 249, D 212, H 473, I 470, M 345, P 320 mm.\n  - Example operating point: 418 m³/h at 166 Pa, 79.7 W.\n  - https://en.ventilatory.net/media/catalog/product/data/ds-kbt-160-ec-en.pdf\n  - The AC version KBT 160E4 is 832 m³/h, 121 W, 24.9 kg: https://en.ventilatory.net/kbt-160e4.html\n- **Systemair KE/KT:** I found no 30-15 size. KT 40-20 is rated 55 °C (snippet).\n\n**3. Grease (flame-protection) filters**\n- **EN 16282-6 F-1 (type A), 500×500×25 mm:** AISI 304, 500 m³/h at 100 Pa, 4.5 kg. A 40 mm-deep version also exists. https://www.gastroplus24.de/de/flammenschutzfilter-typ-a-500-x-500-x-25-mm-ffa505010\n- **EN 16282-6 F-2 (type B), 500×500×20 mm:** 600 m³/h at 50 Pa, 2.4 kg. https://www.gastroplus24.de/de/flammschutzfilter-bauart-b-500-x-500-x-20-mm-nach-din-en-16282-6-f-2/FFO5050-10\n- **Baffle 495×495×45 mm (DIN 18869-5):** 25 Pa at 0.4 m/s, 50 Pa at 0.6 m/s, 80 Pa at 0.7 m/s. At 0.6 m/s that is about 530 m³/h (derived). https://www.ecanopy.co.uk/Box-6-Grease-Filters-Baffle-Commercial-495mm\n- **Manufacturer datasheet (Systemair / Elica / Lamier) with full curves citing EN 16282-6:** NOT FOUND.\n\n**4. Backup power and controller**\n- **Phoenix Contact QUINT4-CAP/24DC/5/4KJ, order no. 2320539:**\n  - 4 kJ in double-layer capacitors, 5 A output.\n  - Buffer time 3 min at 1 A and 30 s at 5 A. At about 25 W (≈1 A) that means roughly 3 min.\n  - 94×130×125 mm (W×H×D), 1243 g, needs 50 mm clearance top and bottom.\n  - Operating −25…+60 °C, derated 1 %/K above 40 °C.\n  - https://dienelectric.com/pdf/Phoenix-Contact-QUINT4-CAP-24DC-5-4KJ---2320539-Datasheet.pdf\n- **RevPi Connect 4:** approved −25…+55 °C, 96×45×110.5 mm, max 20 W. https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Technical_Datasheet_RevPi_Connect-4.pdf\n  - Kunbus says 55 °C is where the processor starts slowing down under load: https://revolutionpi.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=4619\n- **RevPi DIO (100197):** −40…+55 °C, 96×22.5×110.5 mm, 1.5 W, 14 inputs / 14 outputs, 500 mA per output (high-side). https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Datasheet_RevPi_DIO.pdf\n- **Mean Well NDR-120-24:**\n  - Working range −20…+70 °C per its derating curve, 40×125.2×113.5 mm.\n  - Read from the curve drawing (derived): 100 % load from −10 to 50 °C, then straight down to 50 % at 70 °C.\n  - https://docs.rs-online.com/a255/0900766b81621f96.pdf\n\n**5. Thermostats and temperature sensor**\n- **STEGO KTS 011, 01141.0-00** (normally open, closes on rising temperature, 0…60 °C):\n  - 60×33×43 mm, 40 g, 35 mm DIN rail clip, IP20, −45…+80 °C.\n  - Contacts: AC 250 V 10(2) A, AC 120 V 15(2) A, DC 24–72 V 30 W.\n  - Switching difference 7 K ±4 K. The normally-closed version is KTO 011, 01140.0-00.\n  - https://www.tme.eu/Document/9b800d1efeb6c8442e3857b41402ae2b/KTO011_KTS011_EN.pdf\n- **Rittal SK 3110.000:** 71×71×33.5 mm, set range 5…60 °C, change-over contact.\n  - AC 10(4) A heating / AC 5(4) A cooling, DC max 30 W.\n  - Switching difference about 1 K ±0.8 K; 24–230 V AC or 24–60 V DC; 0.105 kg.\n  - https://docs.rs-online.com/49de/A700000008467962.pdf\n- **Sensor option 1, RevPi AIO (100250):** 2 Pt100/Pt1000 inputs (2-, 3- or 4-wire), 96×22.5×110.5 mm, −30…+55 °C. https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Datasheet_RevPi_AIO.pdf\n- **Sensor option 2, Phoenix Contact MINI MCR-SL-PT100-UI-200-NC (2864370):**\n  - 6.2×93.1×102.5 mm, 19.2–30 V DC, &lt;500 mW.\n  - Pt100 input −50…+200 °C (set by switches), 4–20 mA and other outputs.\n  - −20…+65 °C, error &lt;0.3 %.\n  - https://datasheet.octopart.com/2864370-Phoenix-Contact-datasheet-95109.pdf\n\n**6. Heat-transfer data**\n- **ROCKWOOL ProRox PS 960 (ASTM C335):** λ = 0.036 W/mK at 38 °C, 0.042 at 93 °C, 0.050 at 149 °C, 0.058 at 204 °C. Maximum use temperature 649 °C. https://rti.rockwool.com/siteassets/applications/wr-tech/rw-ti-prorox-ps-960-wr-tech_en.pdf\n  - The EN figures (0.046 at 100 °C, 0.064 at 200 °C) are snippet only.\n- **Exhaust temperature at the flue of an electric conveyor oven: NOT FOUND.** Closest data:\n  - Middleby PS638: bakes at 163–316 °C.\n  - Middleby PS638: gives off 15.2 kW to the room at steady 500 °F, 16.0 kW while cooking.\n  - Middleby PS638: oven top skin up to 76.1 °C.\n  - Source: https://www.middlebymarshall.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DOC-1010A-MM-PS638-Ventless-Submittal-Package.pdf\n  - Zanolli Synthesis: maximum set point 320 °C. https://static.ggmgastro.com/Grill_Pizzeria/pizzaofen/dpz/SY1165.E.D.UK.08.rev.0.4_Neutro.pdf\n- **Natural convection in air (laminar):** h = C·(ΔT/L)^0.25, with C = 1.42 for a vertical plate, 1.32 for a horizontal plate heated on top, 0.59 heated underneath. https://www.electronics-cooling.com/2001/08/simplified-formula-for-estimating-natural-convection-heat-transfer-coefficient-on-a-flat-plate/\n  - Example (derived): ΔT 10 K on an 855 mm wall gives h ≈ 2.6 W/m²K.\n  - A vertical plate at ΔT 30 K is about 5 W/m²K (engineersedge, snippet).\n- **Stainless steel emissivity:** polished 0.075, weathered 0.85, type 301 0.54–0.63, at about 300 K. https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/emissivity-coefficients-d_447.html\n  - Buffed 18-8 is 0.16 (snippet). A \"brushed\" value: NOT FOUND.\n\n**7. VRLA battery (why to switch to supercaps)**\n- **CSB GP1272:** nominal 25 °C; discharge −15…50 °C; charge and storage −15…**40 °C**. Design life up to 5 years standby at 25 °C (3–5 years by the European rating). https://csb-battery.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/CSB-Datasheet-GP1272-12V25W-%E2%80%93-053124.pdf\n- **Life halving:** Yuasa says life halves for every 10 °C rise (valid about 15–40 °C) — snippet. https://www.blueboxbatteries.co.uk/assets/yuasa-battery-care-110b.pdf\n  - Schneider gives about 50 % less life per 10 °C above 25 °C (snippet). https://blog.se.com/digital-transformation/it-management/2014/08/28/recommendations-prolonging-life-ups-battery/\n\nWhat this means for the design:\n- A battery charging in a 44–50 °C cabinet is outside CSB's 40 °C charging limit.\n- QUINT4-CAP, NDR-120 and RevPi all work up to 50 °C. The tightest limit is 55 °C, set by the RevPi Connect 4 and DIO.\n- Of the fans, only the KBT 160EC (120 °C) suits the hot hood. The G1G140 (60 °C) and RS 30-15 / IRB (70 °C) are for cooler air only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>249385</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>153</tool_uses><duration_ms>877340</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedInHumanTurn":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user. It is delivered in the same turn as a genuine message from the user — that message IS real user input; respond to it as you normally would.\nDo NOT interpret the notification itself as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nThe notification brings no human input of its own: apart from the user's own messages, any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4269a801e06a0d24</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Wy665uwdLi3pW9q1rNDJRy</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\tasks\\a4269a801e06a0d24.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Research fan, filter, heat data\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I found most of what you asked for, but four things are missing: an exhaust temperature at the flue of an electric conveyor oven, an official ebm-papst 4414 FN sheet, a manufacturer baffle-filter curve that cites EN 16282-6, and a \"brushed stainless\" emissivity. The WebFetch name lookup kept failing on some hosts, so a few values below come only from search-result text and are marked (snippet). Numbers marked (derived) are my own arithmetic.\n\n**1. ebm-papst 4414 F series (official datasheets, all 119×119×25 mm, 0.175 kg)**\n- **4414 FL:** 24 VDC (18–28 V), 1600 rpm, 1.2 W, 94 m³/h, 26 dB(A), −20…+75 °C. Life (L10) is 80 000 h at 40 °C and 35 000 h at maximum temperature. Speed signal output. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414FL-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 F:** 24 V (12–28 V), 2900 rpm, 5.0 W, 170 m³/h, 43 dB(A), maximum 60 °C, L10 60 000 h / 37 500 h. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414F-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 FM:** 2400 rpm, 3.1 W, 140 m³/h, 38 dB(A), maximum 75 °C, L10 70 000 h / 30 000 h. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414FM-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 N:** note it is 119×119×**38** mm. 3650 rpm, 5.4 W, 205 m³/h, 46 dB(A), maximum 70 °C. https://img.ebmpapst.com/products/datasheets/DC-axial-fan-4414N-ENU.pdf\n- **4414 FN:** NOT FOUND. The official URL returns 404.\n\n**2. Duct fans and blowers.** None is made for 300×200; the two rectangular ones are 300×150 and need a transition piece.\n- **(a) ebm-papst G1G140-AV17-02**, 24 VDC blower with spiral housing and flange:\n  - 16–28 V, 54 W, 2.5 A, 1750 rpm, 2.3 kg, IP22, 0–10 V/PWM input plus speed output.\n  - Maximum ambient (and therefore air) temperature is **60 °C**, so it is not suitable for hot hood exhaust.\n  - Outside size max. 227.8×262.6 mm. A distributor listing gives 130 mm depth and about 400 m³/h (235.4 CFM).\n  - https://mm.digikey.com/Volume0/opasdata/d220001/medias/docus/6163/EBMPapstG1G140AV1702datasheet.pdf · https://us.rs-online.com/product/ebm-papst/g1g140-av17-02/70393924/\n- **(b) Systemair RS 30-15 sileo** (item 77284), 300×150 rectangular duct fan:\n  - 230 V, 51 W, 0.224 A, 464 m³/h max, **70 °C** max air temperature (also when speed-controlled), 6.2 kg, IP44.\n  - Dimension letters A–L: 402 / 217 / 340 / 190 / 320 / 170 / 298 / 148 / 79 / 120 / 230 / 254 mm.\n  - Example operating point: 210 m³/h at 228 Pa, 50.8 W.\n  - https://en.ventilatory.net/media/catalog/product/data/ds-rs-30-15-sileo-en.pdf\n- **(c) Soler&amp;Palau IRB/2-180**, 300×150 rectangular duct fan:\n  - 63 W, 0.14 m³/s (504 m³/h), −30…+70 °C, 10 kg.\n  - Table as printed: A1 300, A2 150, B1 320, B2 170, C1 340, C2 190, H1 200, H2 480, L 375 mm.\n  - https://statics.solerpalau.com/media/import/documentation/FINAL_FANS_FOR_FOOD_SERVICE_2020_EDITION_2.pdf (catalogue page 17)\n- **(d) Systemair KBT 160EC** (item 454440), kitchen box fan, **120 °C continuous**:\n  - 230 V, 171 W, 928 m³/h max, 26 kg, Ø160 inlet, 50 mm mineral wool, 0–10 V control, IP55.\n  - Dimension letters: A 437, B 384, C 249, D 212, H 473, I 470, M 345, P 320 mm.\n  - Example operating point: 418 m³/h at 166 Pa, 79.7 W.\n  - https://en.ventilatory.net/media/catalog/product/data/ds-kbt-160-ec-en.pdf\n  - The AC version KBT 160E4 is 832 m³/h, 121 W, 24.9 kg: https://en.ventilatory.net/kbt-160e4.html\n- **Systemair KE/KT:** I found no 30-15 size. KT 40-20 is rated 55 °C (snippet).\n\n**3. Grease (flame-protection) filters**\n- **EN 16282-6 F-1 (type A), 500×500×25 mm:** AISI 304, 500 m³/h at 100 Pa, 4.5 kg. A 40 mm-deep version also exists. https://www.gastroplus24.de/de/flammenschutzfilter-typ-a-500-x-500-x-25-mm-ffa505010\n- **EN 16282-6 F-2 (type B), 500×500×20 mm:** 600 m³/h at 50 Pa, 2.4 kg. https://www.gastroplus24.de/de/flammschutzfilter-bauart-b-500-x-500-x-20-mm-nach-din-en-16282-6-f-2/FFO5050-10\n- **Baffle 495×495×45 mm (DIN 18869-5):** 25 Pa at 0.4 m/s, 50 Pa at 0.6 m/s, 80 Pa at 0.7 m/s. At 0.6 m/s that is about 530 m³/h (derived). https://www.ecanopy.co.uk/Box-6-Grease-Filters-Baffle-Commercial-495mm\n- **Manufacturer datasheet (Systemair / Elica / Lamier) with full curves citing EN 16282-6:** NOT FOUND.\n\n**4. Backup power and controller**\n- **Phoenix Contact QUINT4-CAP/24DC/5/4KJ, order no. 2320539:**\n  - 4 kJ in double-layer capacitors, 5 A output.\n  - Buffer time 3 min at 1 A and 30 s at 5 A. At about 25 W (≈1 A) that means roughly 3 min.\n  - 94×130×125 mm (W×H×D), 1243 g, needs 50 mm clearance top and bottom.\n  - Operating −25…+60 °C, derated 1 %/K above 40 °C.\n  - https://dienelectric.com/pdf/Phoenix-Contact-QUINT4-CAP-24DC-5-4KJ---2320539-Datasheet.pdf\n- **RevPi Connect 4:** approved −25…+55 °C, 96×45×110.5 mm, max 20 W. https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Technical_Datasheet_RevPi_Connect-4.pdf\n  - Kunbus says 55 °C is where the processor starts slowing down under load: https://revolutionpi.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=4619\n- **RevPi DIO (100197):** −40…+55 °C, 96×22.5×110.5 mm, 1.5 W, 14 inputs / 14 outputs, 500 mA per output (high-side). https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Datasheet_RevPi_DIO.pdf\n- **Mean Well NDR-120-24:**\n  - Working range −20…+70 °C per its derating curve, 40×125.2×113.5 mm.\n  - Read from the curve drawing (derived): 100 % load from −10 to 50 °C, then straight down to 50 % at 70 °C.\n  - https://docs.rs-online.com/a255/0900766b81621f96.pdf\n\n**5. Thermostats and temperature sensor**\n- **STEGO KTS 011, 01141.0-00** (normally open, closes on rising temperature, 0…60 °C):\n  - 60×33×43 mm, 40 g, 35 mm DIN rail clip, IP20, −45…+80 °C.\n  - Contacts: AC 250 V 10(2) A, AC 120 V 15(2) A, DC 24–72 V 30 W.\n  - Switching difference 7 K ±4 K. The normally-closed version is KTO 011, 01140.0-00.\n  - https://www.tme.eu/Document/9b800d1efeb6c8442e3857b41402ae2b/KTO011_KTS011_EN.pdf\n- **Rittal SK 3110.000:** 71×71×33.5 mm, set range 5…60 °C, change-over contact.\n  - AC 10(4) A heating / AC 5(4) A cooling, DC max 30 W.\n  - Switching difference about 1 K ±0.8 K; 24–230 V AC or 24–60 V DC; 0.105 kg.\n  - https://docs.rs-online.com/49de/A700000008467962.pdf\n- **Sensor option 1, RevPi AIO (100250):** 2 Pt100/Pt1000 inputs (2-, 3- or 4-wire), 96×22.5×110.5 mm, −30…+55 °C. https://revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/datasheets/Datasheet_RevPi_AIO.pdf\n- **Sensor option 2, Phoenix Contact MINI MCR-SL-PT100-UI-200-NC (2864370):**\n  - 6.2×93.1×102.5 mm, 19.2–30 V DC, &lt;500 mW.\n  - Pt100 input −50…+200 °C (set by switches), 4–20 mA and other outputs.\n  - −20…+65 °C, error &lt;0.3 %.\n  - https://datasheet.octopart.com/2864370-Phoenix-Contact-datasheet-95109.pdf\n\n**6. Heat-transfer data**\n- **ROCKWOOL ProRox PS 960 (ASTM C335):** λ = 0.036 W/mK at 38 °C, 0.042 at 93 °C, 0.050 at 149 °C, 0.058 at 204 °C. Maximum use temperature 649 °C. https://rti.rockwool.com/siteassets/applications/wr-tech/rw-ti-prorox-ps-960-wr-tech_en.pdf\n  - The EN figures (0.046 at 100 °C, 0.064 at 200 °C) are snippet only.\n- **Exhaust temperature at the flue of an electric conveyor oven: NOT FOUND.** Closest data:\n  - Middleby PS638: bakes at 163–316 °C.\n  - Middleby PS638: gives off 15.2 kW to the room at steady 500 °F, 16.0 kW while cooking.\n  - Middleby PS638: oven top skin up to 76.1 °C.\n  - Source: https://www.middlebymarshall.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DOC-1010A-MM-PS638-Ventless-Submittal-Package.pdf\n  - Zanolli Synthesis: maximum set point 320 °C. https://static.ggmgastro.com/Grill_Pizzeria/pizzaofen/dpz/SY1165.E.D.UK.08.rev.0.4_Neutro.pdf\n- **Natural convection in air (laminar):** h = C·(ΔT/L)^0.25, with C = 1.42 for a vertical plate, 1.32 for a horizontal plate heated on top, 0.59 heated underneath. https://www.electronics-cooling.com/2001/08/simplified-formula-for-estimating-natural-convection-heat-transfer-coefficient-on-a-flat-plate/\n  - Example (derived): ΔT 10 K on an 855 mm wall gives h ≈ 2.6 W/m²K.\n  - A vertical plate at ΔT 30 K is about 5 W/m²K (engineersedge, snippet).\n- **Stainless steel emissivity:** polished 0.075, weathered 0.85, type 301 0.54–0.63, at about 300 K. https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/emissivity-coefficients-d_447.html\n  - Buffed 18-8 is 0.16 (snippet). A \"brushed\" value: NOT FOUND.\n\n**7. VRLA battery (why to switch to supercaps)**\n- **CSB GP1272:** nominal 25 °C; discharge −15…50 °C; charge and storage −15…**40 °C**. Design life up to 5 years standby at 25 °C (3–5 years by the European rating). https://csb-battery.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/CSB-Datasheet-GP1272-12V25W-%E2%80%93-053124.pdf\n- **Life halving:** Yuasa says life halves for every 10 °C rise (valid about 15–40 °C) — snippet. https://www.blueboxbatteries.co.uk/assets/yuasa-battery-care-110b.pdf\n  - Schneider gives about 50 % less life per 10 °C above 25 °C (snippet). https://blog.se.com/digital-transformation/it-management/2014/08/28/recommendations-prolonging-life-ups-battery/\n\nWhat this means for the design:\n- A battery charging in a 44–50 °C cabinet is outside CSB's 40 °C charging limit.\n- QUINT4-CAP, NDR-120 and RevPi all work up to 50 °C. The tightest limit is 55 °C, set by the RevPi Connect 4 and DIO.\n- Of the fans, only the KBT 160EC (120 °C) suits the hot hood. The G1G140 (60 °C) and RS 30-15 / IRB (70 °C) are for cooler air only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>249385</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>153</tool_uses><duration_ms>877340</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
{"parentUuid":"7e29c759-be3d-42dc-afb3-95187ec92a9d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab1c8a4a09fa5a796","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14572351 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dd68c1b0-761a-4390-a064-a6c3c870f5f8","timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:46:15.738Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14572351 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
{"parentUuid":"dd68c1b0-761a-4390-a064-a6c3c870f5f8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab1c8a4a09fa5a796","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfcFVUUQdK5TcSQ7CEjR3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395807,"cache_read_input_tokens":38173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":395807,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfcFVTMgjgCJKQEzhN2vz","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf5b0fc0-ca9f-458b-8dd2-182a76732943","timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:47:59.295Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
{"parentUuid":"bf5b0fc0-ca9f-458b-8dd2-182a76732943","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab1c8a4a09fa5a796","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfcFVUUQdK5TcSQ7CEjR3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0173xkcL4QSPxx4We516D2ZD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\firin_ust_v37\\yama_fu.py","content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"v3.7 · h3_firin_ust_v1.py: davlumbaz fanı (Systemair RS 30-15 sileo) + dikey kanal + EN 16282-6 yağ filtresi + aktif karbon kaseti\"\"\"\nimport os\nS = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\np = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(S), \"b3\", \"arastirma\", \"_uretec\", \"h3\", \"h3_firin_ust_v1.py\")\ns = open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n\n\ndef R(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == n, (a[:90], s.count(a)); s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n\nR('''    Tavan sacı altı 1860,5 · motor üstü 1838 + 20 = 1858 → 2,5 mm boşluk (servis: kompresör düz raf üstünde öne kayar, kaldırma gerekmez).\"\"\"''',\n  '''    Tavan sacı altı 1860,5 · motor üstü 1838 + 20 = 1858 → 2,5 mm boşluk (servis: kompresör düz raf üstünde öne kayar, kaldırma gerekmez).\nv3.7 (1 Eki 2026 · Claude · YEREL) — DAVLUMBAZ FANI + FİLTRELER (eksik taraması: F_DAVLUMBAZ kutusunda fan / filtre yoktu · bizim parçamız, fırın DEĞİL):\n  AKIŞ: davlumbaz kutusu ön yüzündeki 9 emiş yarığı (x 3390–3950 · y 1520–1730, kompresörün arkası) → EN 16282-6 yağ (alev) filtresi 500 × 400 × 25 AISI 304\n  → aktif karbon kaseti 500 × 400 × 30 → kutu içi plenum → FAN Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (300 × 150 dikdörtgen kanal fanı · 230 V 51 W · 464 m³/h maks ·\n  hava ≤ 70 °C · 6,2 kg · föy ds-rs-30-15-sileo) yatay, emişi +x (plenuma) → dikey kanal 300 × 200 (kutu içinde y 1330 → 1790, yan ağzı 298 × 148) →\n  atış kanalı (FU0) → U_F baca uzantısı → bina. ÇALIŞMA NOKTASI (föy): 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa (filtre ~100 + karbon ~80 + kanal / bina ~50 Pa — VARSAYIM) ·\n  gereken ≈ 195 m³/h (F kabini ısı yükü ≈ 600 W VARSAYIM, oda + 10 K) · fan altta 2 konsolda, davlumbaz tabanına vidalı. Fan kablosu: arka sacın\n  'davlumbaz_fani' M20 rakoru (x 2600 · y 1825) → fan klemens kutusu (sözleşme DAV_FAN_KLEMENS) · 230 V besleme kaynağı AÇIK (ana panoda raf yeri yok).\n  ⚠ RS 30-15 hava sınırı 70 °C: davlumbaz F kabini havasını emer (yanma gazı yok · elektrikli fırın); fırın tünel buharı > 70 °C ise Systemair KBT 160EC\n  (120 °C, 26 kg, 437 × 384 × 473) kutuya SIĞMAZ (iç yükseklik 472) → kutu büyütülmeli (Kemal kararı).\"\"\"''')\n\nR('''def kur():\n    FU0.kur()\n    PARCALAR[:] = [p for p in PARCALAR if not p[\"ad\"].startswith(F_KOMP_DUS)]\n    kompresor_ayaklari_v36()\n    return PARCALAR''', '''# ================================================================ v3.7 · DAVLUMBAZ FANI + FİLTRELER ================================================================\nDAV_IC = (FU0.DAV[0] + FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[1] - FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[2] + FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[3] - FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[4] + FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[5] - FU0.SAC)   # 2503–3997 · 1316,5–1788,5 · −825,5…−441,5\nDIKEY = dict(x=(2952.0, 3248.0), y=(1330.0, 1790.0), z=(-718.0, -522.0), t=1.5)          # kutu içi dikey kanal (üstü atış ağzına geçer, FU0 atış kanalı 1790'da başlar)\nFAN_RS = dict(L=402.0, fl=15.0, gov=(340.0, 190.0), fl_dis=(320.0, 170.0), fl_ic=(298.0, 148.0), kk=(80.0, 60.0, 27.0))   # Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (föy harf ölçüleri A 402 · C 340 · D 190 · E 320 · F 170 · G 298 · H 148 · B 217 = gövde + klemens kutusu) — harf eşlemesi VARSAYIM\nFAN_YC, FAN_ZC = 1491.0, -620.0                                                            # kanal ekseni (ağız 298 dik y · 148 z)\nFAN_X0 = DIKEY[\"x\"][1]                                                                      # çıkış flanşı dikey kanalın +x yüzüne dayanır (3248) · emiş 3650'de +x'e bakar\nFILTRE_YAG = dict(x=(3420.0, 3920.0), y=(1350.0, 1750.0), t=25.0)                           # EN 16282-6 tip A · 500 × 400 × 25 (ölçü listeden VARSAYIM; 500 × 500 kutuya sığmaz: iç 472)\nKARBON_T = 30.0\nCERCEVE = dict(x=(3385.0, 3955.0), y=(1335.0, 1765.0))                                       # filtre çerçevesi: emiş yarıklarını (3390–3950 · 1520–1730) tamamen örter → by-pass yok\nDAV_FAN_KLEMENS = (3460.0, 1490.0, FAN_ZC - FAN_RS[\"gov\"][1] / 2.0 - FAN_RS[\"kk\"][2])      # elektrik ajanı: fan klemens kutusunun dış yüzü (−z)\n\n\ndef davlumbaz_v37():\n    B = \"F_DAVLUMBAZ\"\n    x0, x1, y0, y1, z0, z1 = DAV_IC\n    # ---- dikey kanal (kutu içi): 304 1,5 · alt kapalı · +x yüzünde fan ağzı 298 × 148 ----\n    dx0, dx1 = DIKEY[\"x\"]; dy0, dy1 = DIKEY[\"y\"]; dz0, dz1 = DIKEY[\"z\"]; t = DIKEY[\"t\"]\n    dk = FU0.kut(dx0, dx1, dy0, dy1, dz0, dz1).cut(FU0.kut(dx0 + t, dx1 - t, dy0 + t, dy1 + 1.0, dz0 + t, dz1 - t))\n    gy, gz = FAN_RS[\"fl_ic\"]\n    dk = dk.cut(FU0.kut(dx1 - t - 1.0, dx1 + 1.0, FAN_YC - gy / 2.0, FAN_YC + gy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - gz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + gz / 2.0))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_dikey_kanal\", dk, \"sac\", B, kaynak=\"v3.7\",\n             bom=(\"Davlumbaz dikey kanalı 304 1,5 · 296 × 196 × 460 · alt kapalı · yanda 298 × 148 fan ağzı\", 1, \"abkant + kaynak\",\n                  \"v3.7 · üstü kutunun atış ağzına geçer (atış kanalı 1790'da) · alt ucu kutu tabanına 2 köşebentle\", \"ÜRETİM\"))\n    for i, xa in enumerate((dx0 + 20.0, dx1 - 50.0)):\n        FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_dikey_kanal_ayagi_%d\" % i, FU0.kut(xa, xa + 30.0, y0, dy0, dz0 + 20.0, dz1 - 20.0), \"paslanmaz\", B,\n                 bom=(\"Dikey kanal ayağı 304 kutu 30 × 13,5 × 156\", 2, \"kesim\", \"kutu tabanına kaynaklı\", \"ÜRETİM\") if i == 0 else None)\n    # ---- fan RS 30-15 (yatay · x boyunca · çıkış −x → dikey kanal · emiş +x) ----\n    L, fl = FAN_RS[\"L\"], FAN_RS[\"fl\"]; cy, cz = FAN_RS[\"gov\"]; ey, ez = FAN_RS[\"fl_dis\"]; iy, iz = FAN_RS[\"fl_ic\"]\n    fa, fb = FAN_X0, FAN_X0 + L\n    fan = FU0.kut(fa + fl, fb - fl, FAN_YC - cy / 2.0, FAN_YC + cy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - cz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + cz / 2.0)\n    for xa_, xb_ in ((fa, fa + fl), (fb - fl, fb)):\n        fan = fan.union(FU0.kut(xa_, xb_, FAN_YC - ey / 2.0, FAN_YC + ey / 2.0, FAN_ZC - ez / 2.0, FAN_ZC + ez / 2.0))\n    fan = fan.cut(FU0.kut(fa - 1.0, fa + fl + 5.0, FAN_YC - iy / 2.0, FAN_YC + iy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - iz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + iz / 2.0))     # çıkış ağzı\n    fan = fan.cut(FU0.kut(fb - fl - 5.0, fb + 1.0, FAN_YC - iy / 2.0, FAN_YC + iy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - iz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + iz / 2.0))     # emiş ağzı\n    kx, ky, kz = FAN_RS[\"kk\"]\n    fan = fan.union(FU0.kut(DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[0] - kx / 2.0, DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[0] + kx / 2.0, DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[1] - ky / 2.0, DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[1] + ky / 2.0,\n                            DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[2], FAN_ZC - cz / 2.0))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_fani_Systemair_RS_30-15_sileo\", fan, \"celik\", B,\n             kaynak=\"Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (77284) · föy ds-rs-30-15-sileo-en.pdf: 230 V 51 W · 464 m³/h · hava ≤ 70 °C · 6,2 kg · 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa\",\n             bom=(\"Davlumbaz fanı Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (77284) · dikdörtgen kanal fanı 300 × 150 · 230 V 51 W · 464 m³/h · ≤ 70 °C\", 1,\n                  \"katalog (systemair.com) · dış ölçü föy harfleri A 402 · C 340 · D 190 · E 320 · F 170 (eşleme VARSAYIM)\",\n                  \"v3.7 · çalışma 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa (föy) · hız kontrolü (5 kademe trafo / tristör) · 230 V besleme AÇIK\", \"SATIN ALMA\"))\n    for i, xa in enumerate((fa + 50.0, fb - 80.0)):\n        FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_fan_konsolu_%d\" % i, FU0.kut(xa, xa + 30.0, y0, FAN_YC - cy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - cz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + cz / 2.0), \"paslanmaz\", B,\n                 bom=(\"Fan konsolu 304 lama 30 × 4,5 × 190 (kutu tabanına kaynaklı, fana 2 × M8 titreşim takozlu)\", 2, \"kesim\", \"\", \"ÜRETİM\") if i == 0 else None)\n    # ---- filtre çerçevesi + EN 16282-6 yağ filtresi + aktif karbon kaseti (emiş yarıklarının arkası) ----\n    zf1 = z1; zf0 = zf1 - FILTRE_YAG[\"t\"]; zk0 = zf0 - KARBON_T\n    fx0, fx1 = FILTRE_YAG[\"x\"]; fy0, fy1 = FILTRE_YAG[\"y\"]\n    cer = FU0.kut(CERCEVE[\"x\"][0], CERCEVE[\"x\"][1], CERCEVE[\"y\"][0], CERCEVE[\"y\"][1], zk0, zf1).cut(FU0.kut(fx0, fx1, fy0, fy1, zk0 - 1.0, zf1 + 1.0))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_filtre_cercevesi\", cer, \"paslanmaz\", B,\n             bom=(\"Filtre çerçevesi 304 1,5 (U ray, önden sürme) · 570 × 430 × 55\", 1, \"abkant + kaynak\", \"v3.7 · ön yüz iç tarafına perçin · emiş yarıklarının hepsini örter (by-pass yok)\", \"ÜRETİM\"))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_yag_filtresi_EN16282\", FU0.kut(fx0, fx1, fy0, fy1, zf0, zf1), \"paslanmaz\", B,\n             kaynak=\"EN 16282-6 tip A (F-1) alev / yağ filtresi AISI 304 · 500 × 500 × 25 föyü: 500 m³/h @ 100 Pa (gastroplus24) — 500 × 400 boyu VARSAYIM\",\n             bom=(\"Yağ (alev) filtresi EN 16282-6 tip A · AISI 304 labirent · 500 × 400 × 25\", 1, \"katalog · bulaşık makinesinde yıkanır\",\n                  \"v3.7 · 500 × 500 standardı kutuya sığmaz (iç yükseklik 472) → 500 × 400 (ölçü teyit)\", \"SATIN ALMA\"))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_karbon_filtre\", FU0.kut(fx0, fx1, fy0, fy1, zk0, zf0), \"koyu\", B,\n             bom=(\"Aktif karbon kaseti 500 × 400 × 30 (koku)\", 1, \"sarf · 3–6 ayda değişim\", \"v3.7 · ölçü / basınç kaybı VARSAYIM (~80 Pa)\", \"SARF\"))\n\n\ndef kur():\n    FU0.kur()\n    PARCALAR[:] = [p for p in PARCALAR if not p[\"ad\"].startswith(F_KOMP_DUS)]\n    kompresor_ayaklari_v36()\n    davlumbaz_v37()\n    return PARCALAR''')\n\nR('''BIRIMLER = [(k, a) if k != \"F_KOMP_AYAK\" else''', '''BIRIMLER = [(k, a) if k not in (\"F_KOMP_AYAK\", \"F_DAVLUMBAZ\") else\n            (\"F_DAVLUMBAZ\", \"Davlumbaz (bizim) · 304 1,5 kutu x 2501,5–3998,5 · y 1315–1790 · z −827…−440 · v3.7: EN 16282-6 yağ filtresi 500 × 400 + aktif karbon (emiş yarıklarının arkası) · \"\n                            \"Systemair RS 30-15 sileo kanal fanı (230 V 51 W · 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa) → kutu içi dikey kanal 300 × 200 → atış kanalı → U_F baca\") if k == \"F_DAVLUMBAZ\" else''')\nopen(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nprint(\"fu yama tamam\")\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395807,"cache_read_input_tokens":38173,"output_tokens":15017,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":9055},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":395807},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15017,"cache_read_input_tokens":38173,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":395807,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0173xkcL4QSPxx4We516D2ZD":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\firin_ust_v37\\yama_fu.py","content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"v3.7 · h3_firin_ust_v1.py: davlumbaz fanı (Systemair RS 30-15 sileo) + dikey kanal + EN 16282-6 yağ filtresi + aktif karbon kaseti\"\"\"\nimport os\nS = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\np = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(S), \"b3\", \"arastirma\", \"_uretec\", \"h3\", \"h3_firin_ust_v1.py\")\ns = open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n\n\ndef R(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == n, (a[:90], s.count(a)); s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n\nR('''    Tavan sacı altı 1860,5 · motor üstü 1838 + 20 = 1858 → 2,5 mm boşluk (servis: kompresör düz raf üstünde öne kayar, kaldırma gerekmez).\"\"\"''',\n  '''    Tavan sacı altı 1860,5 · motor üstü 1838 + 20 = 1858 → 2,5 mm boşluk (servis: kompresör düz raf üstünde öne kayar, kaldırma gerekmez).\nv3.7 (1 Eki 2026 · Claude · YEREL) — DAVLUMBAZ FANI + FİLTRELER (eksik taraması: F_DAVLUMBAZ kutusunda fan / filtre yoktu · bizim parçamız, fırın DEĞİL):\n  AKIŞ: davlumbaz kutusu ön yüzündeki 9 emiş yarığı (x 3390–3950 · y 1520–1730, kompresörün arkası) → EN 16282-6 yağ (alev) filtresi 500 × 400 × 25 AISI 304\n  → aktif karbon kaseti 500 × 400 × 30 → kutu içi plenum → FAN Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (300 × 150 dikdörtgen kanal fanı · 230 V 51 W · 464 m³/h maks ·\n  hava ≤ 70 °C · 6,2 kg · föy ds-rs-30-15-sileo) yatay, emişi +x (plenuma) → dikey kanal 300 × 200 (kutu içinde y 1330 → 1790, yan ağzı 298 × 148) →\n  atış kanalı (FU0) → U_F baca uzantısı → bina. ÇALIŞMA NOKTASI (föy): 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa (filtre ~100 + karbon ~80 + kanal / bina ~50 Pa — VARSAYIM) ·\n  gereken ≈ 195 m³/h (F kabini ısı yükü ≈ 600 W VARSAYIM, oda + 10 K) · fan altta 2 konsolda, davlumbaz tabanına vidalı. Fan kablosu: arka sacın\n  'davlumbaz_fani' M20 rakoru (x 2600 · y 1825) → fan klemens kutusu (sözleşme DAV_FAN_KLEMENS) · 230 V besleme kaynağı AÇIK (ana panoda raf yeri yok).\n  ⚠ RS 30-15 hava sınırı 70 °C: davlumbaz F kabini havasını emer (yanma gazı yok · elektrikli fırın); fırın tünel buharı > 70 °C ise Systemair KBT 160EC\n  (120 °C, 26 kg, 437 × 384 × 473) kutuya SIĞMAZ (iç yükseklik 472) → kutu büyütülmeli (Kemal kararı).\"\"\"''')\n\nR('''def kur():\n    FU0.kur()\n    PARCALAR[:] = [p for p in PARCALAR if not p[\"ad\"].startswith(F_KOMP_DUS)]\n    kompresor_ayaklari_v36()\n    return PARCALAR''', '''# ================================================================ v3.7 · DAVLUMBAZ FANI + FİLTRELER ================================================================\nDAV_IC = (FU0.DAV[0] + FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[1] - FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[2] + FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[3] - FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[4] + FU0.SAC, FU0.DAV[5] - FU0.SAC)   # 2503–3997 · 1316,5–1788,5 · −825,5…−441,5\nDIKEY = dict(x=(2952.0, 3248.0), y=(1330.0, 1790.0), z=(-718.0, -522.0), t=1.5)          # kutu içi dikey kanal (üstü atış ağzına geçer, FU0 atış kanalı 1790'da başlar)\nFAN_RS = dict(L=402.0, fl=15.0, gov=(340.0, 190.0), fl_dis=(320.0, 170.0), fl_ic=(298.0, 148.0), kk=(80.0, 60.0, 27.0))   # Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (föy harf ölçüleri A 402 · C 340 · D 190 · E 320 · F 170 · G 298 · H 148 · B 217 = gövde + klemens kutusu) — harf eşlemesi VARSAYIM\nFAN_YC, FAN_ZC = 1491.0, -620.0                                                            # kanal ekseni (ağız 298 dik y · 148 z)\nFAN_X0 = DIKEY[\"x\"][1]                                                                      # çıkış flanşı dikey kanalın +x yüzüne dayanır (3248) · emiş 3650'de +x'e bakar\nFILTRE_YAG = dict(x=(3420.0, 3920.0), y=(1350.0, 1750.0), t=25.0)                           # EN 16282-6 tip A · 500 × 400 × 25 (ölçü listeden VARSAYIM; 500 × 500 kutuya sığmaz: iç 472)\nKARBON_T = 30.0\nCERCEVE = dict(x=(3385.0, 3955.0), y=(1335.0, 1765.0))                                       # filtre çerçevesi: emiş yarıklarını (3390–3950 · 1520–1730) tamamen örter → by-pass yok\nDAV_FAN_KLEMENS = (3460.0, 1490.0, FAN_ZC - FAN_RS[\"gov\"][1] / 2.0 - FAN_RS[\"kk\"][2])      # elektrik ajanı: fan klemens kutusunun dış yüzü (−z)\n\n\ndef davlumbaz_v37():\n    B = \"F_DAVLUMBAZ\"\n    x0, x1, y0, y1, z0, z1 = DAV_IC\n    # ---- dikey kanal (kutu içi): 304 1,5 · alt kapalı · +x yüzünde fan ağzı 298 × 148 ----\n    dx0, dx1 = DIKEY[\"x\"]; dy0, dy1 = DIKEY[\"y\"]; dz0, dz1 = DIKEY[\"z\"]; t = DIKEY[\"t\"]\n    dk = FU0.kut(dx0, dx1, dy0, dy1, dz0, dz1).cut(FU0.kut(dx0 + t, dx1 - t, dy0 + t, dy1 + 1.0, dz0 + t, dz1 - t))\n    gy, gz = FAN_RS[\"fl_ic\"]\n    dk = dk.cut(FU0.kut(dx1 - t - 1.0, dx1 + 1.0, FAN_YC - gy / 2.0, FAN_YC + gy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - gz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + gz / 2.0))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_dikey_kanal\", dk, \"sac\", B, kaynak=\"v3.7\",\n             bom=(\"Davlumbaz dikey kanalı 304 1,5 · 296 × 196 × 460 · alt kapalı · yanda 298 × 148 fan ağzı\", 1, \"abkant + kaynak\",\n                  \"v3.7 · üstü kutunun atış ağzına geçer (atış kanalı 1790'da) · alt ucu kutu tabanına 2 köşebentle\", \"ÜRETİM\"))\n    for i, xa in enumerate((dx0 + 20.0, dx1 - 50.0)):\n        FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_dikey_kanal_ayagi_%d\" % i, FU0.kut(xa, xa + 30.0, y0, dy0, dz0 + 20.0, dz1 - 20.0), \"paslanmaz\", B,\n                 bom=(\"Dikey kanal ayağı 304 kutu 30 × 13,5 × 156\", 2, \"kesim\", \"kutu tabanına kaynaklı\", \"ÜRETİM\") if i == 0 else None)\n    # ---- fan RS 30-15 (yatay · x boyunca · çıkış −x → dikey kanal · emiş +x) ----\n    L, fl = FAN_RS[\"L\"], FAN_RS[\"fl\"]; cy, cz = FAN_RS[\"gov\"]; ey, ez = FAN_RS[\"fl_dis\"]; iy, iz = FAN_RS[\"fl_ic\"]\n    fa, fb = FAN_X0, FAN_X0 + L\n    fan = FU0.kut(fa + fl, fb - fl, FAN_YC - cy / 2.0, FAN_YC + cy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - cz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + cz / 2.0)\n    for xa_, xb_ in ((fa, fa + fl), (fb - fl, fb)):\n        fan = fan.union(FU0.kut(xa_, xb_, FAN_YC - ey / 2.0, FAN_YC + ey / 2.0, FAN_ZC - ez / 2.0, FAN_ZC + ez / 2.0))\n    fan = fan.cut(FU0.kut(fa - 1.0, fa + fl + 5.0, FAN_YC - iy / 2.0, FAN_YC + iy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - iz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + iz / 2.0))     # çıkış ağzı\n    fan = fan.cut(FU0.kut(fb - fl - 5.0, fb + 1.0, FAN_YC - iy / 2.0, FAN_YC + iy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - iz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + iz / 2.0))     # emiş ağzı\n    kx, ky, kz = FAN_RS[\"kk\"]\n    fan = fan.union(FU0.kut(DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[0] - kx / 2.0, DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[0] + kx / 2.0, DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[1] - ky / 2.0, DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[1] + ky / 2.0,\n                            DAV_FAN_KLEMENS[2], FAN_ZC - cz / 2.0))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_fani_Systemair_RS_30-15_sileo\", fan, \"celik\", B,\n             kaynak=\"Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (77284) · föy ds-rs-30-15-sileo-en.pdf: 230 V 51 W · 464 m³/h · hava ≤ 70 °C · 6,2 kg · 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa\",\n             bom=(\"Davlumbaz fanı Systemair RS 30-15 sileo (77284) · dikdörtgen kanal fanı 300 × 150 · 230 V 51 W · 464 m³/h · ≤ 70 °C\", 1,\n                  \"katalog (systemair.com) · dış ölçü föy harfleri A 402 · C 340 · D 190 · E 320 · F 170 (eşleme VARSAYIM)\",\n                  \"v3.7 · çalışma 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa (föy) · hız kontrolü (5 kademe trafo / tristör) · 230 V besleme AÇIK\", \"SATIN ALMA\"))\n    for i, xa in enumerate((fa + 50.0, fb - 80.0)):\n        FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_fan_konsolu_%d\" % i, FU0.kut(xa, xa + 30.0, y0, FAN_YC - cy / 2.0, FAN_ZC - cz / 2.0, FAN_ZC + cz / 2.0), \"paslanmaz\", B,\n                 bom=(\"Fan konsolu 304 lama 30 × 4,5 × 190 (kutu tabanına kaynaklı, fana 2 × M8 titreşim takozlu)\", 2, \"kesim\", \"\", \"ÜRETİM\") if i == 0 else None)\n    # ---- filtre çerçevesi + EN 16282-6 yağ filtresi + aktif karbon kaseti (emiş yarıklarının arkası) ----\n    zf1 = z1; zf0 = zf1 - FILTRE_YAG[\"t\"]; zk0 = zf0 - KARBON_T\n    fx0, fx1 = FILTRE_YAG[\"x\"]; fy0, fy1 = FILTRE_YAG[\"y\"]\n    cer = FU0.kut(CERCEVE[\"x\"][0], CERCEVE[\"x\"][1], CERCEVE[\"y\"][0], CERCEVE[\"y\"][1], zk0, zf1).cut(FU0.kut(fx0, fx1, fy0, fy1, zk0 - 1.0, zf1 + 1.0))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_filtre_cercevesi\", cer, \"paslanmaz\", B,\n             bom=(\"Filtre çerçevesi 304 1,5 (U ray, önden sürme) · 570 × 430 × 55\", 1, \"abkant + kaynak\", \"v3.7 · ön yüz iç tarafına perçin · emiş yarıklarının hepsini örter (by-pass yok)\", \"ÜRETİM\"))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_yag_filtresi_EN16282\", FU0.kut(fx0, fx1, fy0, fy1, zf0, zf1), \"paslanmaz\", B,\n             kaynak=\"EN 16282-6 tip A (F-1) alev / yağ filtresi AISI 304 · 500 × 500 × 25 föyü: 500 m³/h @ 100 Pa (gastroplus24) — 500 × 400 boyu VARSAYIM\",\n             bom=(\"Yağ (alev) filtresi EN 16282-6 tip A · AISI 304 labirent · 500 × 400 × 25\", 1, \"katalog · bulaşık makinesinde yıkanır\",\n                  \"v3.7 · 500 × 500 standardı kutuya sığmaz (iç yükseklik 472) → 500 × 400 (ölçü teyit)\", \"SATIN ALMA\"))\n    FU0.ekle(\"f_davlumbaz_karbon_filtre\", FU0.kut(fx0, fx1, fy0, fy1, zk0, zf0), \"koyu\", B,\n             bom=(\"Aktif karbon kaseti 500 × 400 × 30 (koku)\", 1, \"sarf · 3–6 ayda değişim\", \"v3.7 · ölçü / basınç kaybı VARSAYIM (~80 Pa)\", \"SARF\"))\n\n\ndef kur():\n    FU0.kur()\n    PARCALAR[:] = [p for p in PARCALAR if not p[\"ad\"].startswith(F_KOMP_DUS)]\n    kompresor_ayaklari_v36()\n    davlumbaz_v37()\n    return PARCALAR''')\n\nR('''BIRIMLER = [(k, a) if k != \"F_KOMP_AYAK\" else''', '''BIRIMLER = [(k, a) if k not in (\"F_KOMP_AYAK\", \"F_DAVLUMBAZ\") else\n            (\"F_DAVLUMBAZ\", \"Davlumbaz (bizim) · 304 1,5 kutu x 2501,5–3998,5 · y 1315–1790 · z −827…−440 · v3.7: EN 16282-6 yağ filtresi 500 × 400 + aktif karbon (emiş yarıklarının arkası) · \"\n                            \"Systemair RS 30-15 sileo kanal fanı (230 V 51 W · 210 m³/h @ 228 Pa) → kutu içi dikey kanal 300 × 200 → atış kanalı → U_F baca\") if k == \"F_DAVLUMBAZ\" else''')\nopen(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nprint(\"fu yama tamam\")\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfcFVTMgjgCJKQEzhN2vz","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4411a18e-9131-409f-a21b-df2fd8480503","timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:48:47.049Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
